-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/647c8abf-9979-539d-a065-2dcc2bc9014b
-- title:
--   Spectral comparison of cut traces in prime-degree Galois extensions
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L/K$ an extension of number fields which is Galois and whose degree $n = [L:K]$ is prime (`hdeg`), $\sigma$ is a $K$-automorphism of $L$ with $\sigma \neq 1$ (`hσ`) such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the cyclic group generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (`hgen`), and $D$ is an idele Galois descent datum for $L/K$, i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of the adele ring of $L$ which is compatible with the structure map from $L$ and continuous for each automorphism. All measure-theoretic and Borel structures on $GL_2$ of the adeles and on the idele groups are the Borel ones attached to the adelic topologies.
--
--   **Geometric domain over $K$.** Real parameters $c_K, u_K, d_{1K}, d_{2K}$ are given with $0 < c_K$ (`hcK`) and $0 < d_{1K} < d_{2K}$ (`hd₁K`, `hdK`), together with a finite set $T_K$ of points of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$. The hypothesis `hcovK` asserts that the union $\bigcup_{x \in T_K}$ of the right translates by $x$ of the centre-cut Siegel set `centreCutSiegelSet K cK uK d₁K d₂K` — the set of $g$ whose finite part lies in the finite integral subgroup and whose archimedean component at every infinite place has local height at least $c_K$, $x$-window square at most $u_K^2$ and archimedean determinant norm in $[d_{1K}, d_{2K}]$ — covers $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ modulo the centre, in the sense that every $g$ admits $\gamma \in GL_2(K)$ and an idele $z$ with $\gamma\, g\, z$ (global point on the left, central scalar on the right) lying in that union.
--
--   **Determinant slabs and fundamental domains.** Reals $\alpha, \beta$ satisfy $0 < \alpha < \beta$ (`hα`, `hαβ`). The set $\Phi_L \subseteq GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ is contained in the slab $\{g : \|\det g\|_{\mathbb{A}_L} \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΦs`) and is a fundamental domain (`hΦ`) for the left action of the image of $GL_2(L)$ on that slab, for the adelic Haar measure of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ restricted to it; likewise $\Phi_K$ lies in the corresponding slab over $K$ (`hΦKs`) and is a fundamental domain for the image of $GL_2(K)$ (`hΦK`).
--
--   **Sets of primes.** $S_K$ and $S_L$ are finite sets of primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and of $\mathcal{O}_L$ with: every prime $w$ of $L$ lying over a prime of $S_K$ belongs to $S_L$ (`hSL`); membership in $S_L$ depends only on the prime of $K$ below, i.e. $w \in S_L \iff w' \in S_L$ whenever $w$ and $w'$ lie over the same prime (`hSsat`); and every prime $w$ of $L$ whose prime below is outside $S_K$ has ramification index $1$ (`hS`).
--
--   **Central characters.** $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full unit group of the adeles of $L$ (taken as the top subgroup) to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ which is continuous (`hξc`), trivial on the principal ideles, i.e. on the image of $L^\times$ (`hξt`), and takes the same value on $\det$ of the adelic Hecke generators `heckeGen (𝓞 L) L w` and `heckeGen (𝓞 L) L w'` for any two primes $w, w' \notin S_L$ over the same prime of $K$ (`hξσ`). $\Xi$ is a finite set of characters of the idele group of $K$, and `hΞ` states that $\Xi$ consists exactly of those characters $\xi$ which are continuous, trivial on the principal ideles of $K$, and satisfy $\xi(\mathcal{N}(z)) = \xi_L(z)$ for all ideles $z$ of $L$, where $\mathcal{N}$ is the idelic norm of the base-change datum [`M4aHerbrand.GenuineDescent.genuineBaseChange K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineDescent.html#L87).
--
--   **Levels.** $N$ is an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_L$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S_L$ (`hN`), and $N'$ an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S_K$ (`hN'`).
--
--   **Test functions and matching.** $\mathrm{tys}_L$ is an archimedean type family for $L$ and $\varphi : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ is continuous (`hφ`) with compact support (`hφc`) satisfying `IsUnitFactorizableAboveOfType K L tysL (levelOne (𝓞 L) L N ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L) SK φ`, that is: $\varphi$ satisfies the predicate `IsUnitFactorizableAbove` relative to $S_K$ at the level given by the intersection of the level-one subgroup of $N$ with the kernel of the archimedean projection, and $\varphi$ is archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_L$ (`IsArchBiFinite`: $x \mapsto \varphi(x^{-1})$ lies in the archimedean cut submodule of $\mathrm{tys}_L$ and $\varphi$ lies in the dual one). Similarly $\mathrm{tys}_K$ is an archimedean type family for $K$ and $f : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K) \to \mathbb{C}$ is continuous (`hf`) with compact support (`hfc`) satisfying `IsUnitFactorizableOfTypeAt K tysK (principalLevel (𝓞 K) K N' ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K) SK f`: $f$ is bi-invariant under the intersection of the principal congruence subgroup of $N'$ with the kernel of the archimedean projection, factors as an archimedean test factor times a finite test factor whose value is the product of local test functions at the primes of $S_K$ when all components outside $S_K$ are integral units and is zero otherwise, and $f$ is archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_K$. Finally `hm` asserts `AreMatchingAt K L σ.symm SK φ f`: there are factorizations of $\varphi$ (archimedean, finite and semi-local factors, `IsSemiLocalFactorization`) and of $f$ (`IsUnitFactorization`) with matching archimedean factors and with the semi-local and local factors matching at every $v \in S_K$ in the sense of `AreMatchingLocal K L v σ.symm`, i.e. coupled $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted orbital integrals against ordinary orbital integrals at regular semisimple classes, for the semi-local and local Haar measures, together with the vanishing of the orbital integrals of the $K$-side function at regular semisimple classes which are not norms.
--
--   **Fundamental-lemma inputs.** Three hypotheses supply local transfer outside $S_K$.
--   `hFLu`: for every $v \notin S_K$ such that every prime of $L$ above $v$ has ramification index $1$, the indicator function of the semi-local integral units of $L \otimes_K K_v$ and the indicator function of the integral units of $GL_2(K_v)$ are matching in the sense of `AreMatchingLocal K L v σ.symm`.
--   `hFLs` (split case): for every $v \notin S_K$, every $K_v$-algebra isomorphism $e : L \otimes_K K_v \cong K_v^{\,n}$, every index $i_0$, every subgroup $U$ equal to the integral subgroup [`LocalGL2.integralSubgroup`](def/LocalLanglands_LocalHeckeInstance.html#L13) of $GL_2(K_v)$, and every element $f_1$ of the Hecke algebra of $U$ over $\mathbb{C}$, the function on $GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ sending $g$ to $f_1$ evaluated at the $i_0$-th component of $e(g)$, multiplied by the indicator of the set of elements all of whose remaining components lie in $U$, is matching with $f_1$ itself.
--   `hFLi` (unramified-prime case): for every $v \notin S_K$, every extension $w$ of $v$ to $L$ with ramification index $1$, every $K_v$-algebra isomorphism $e : L \otimes_K K_v \cong L_w$, irreducible uniformisers $\varpi_K$ of the valuation ring of $K_v$ and $\varpi_L$ of that of $L_w$ with nonzero images, the integral subgroups $U_K \le GL_2(K_v)$ and $U_L \le GL_2(L_w)$, elements $T_v, E_v$ of the Hecke algebra of $U_K$ over $\mathbb{C}$ whose underlying functions are the indicator of the double coset $U_K\,\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_K,1)\,U_K$ and $\mathrm{N}(v)$ times the indicator of $\varpi_K U_K$ respectively, the analogous elements $T_w, E_w$ for $U_L$ with $\mathrm{N}(w)$, and any sequence $p$ in the Hecke algebra of $U_K$ with $p_0 = 2$, $p_1 = T_v$ and $p_{k+2} = T_v p_{k+1} - E_v p_k$: there exists a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra homomorphism $b$ from the Hecke algebra of $U_L$ to that of $U_K$ with $b(T_w) = p_n$, $b(E_w) = E_v^{\,n}$, and such that for every element $\psi$ of the Hecke algebra of $U_L$ the function $g \mapsto \psi(e(g))$ on $GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ and $b(\psi)$ are matching in the sense of `AreMatchingLocal K L v σ.symm`.
--
--   **Central data.** $\nu_{Z,L}$ and $\nu_{Z,K}$ are Haar measures on the idele groups of $L$ and of $K$, and $\Omega_L$, $\Omega_K$ are fundamental domains for the action of the principal ideles on them (`hΩL`, `hΩK`).
--
--   **Comparison of geometric sides (`hgeo`).** There exists $c \neq 0$ such that for every finite set $S' \supseteq S_K$ of primes of $K$ and every pair of functions $\varphi$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $f$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, continuous with compact support, with $\varphi$ unit-factorizable above $K$ relative to $S'$ of type $\mathrm{tys}_L$ at the level of $N$, with $f$ unit-factorizable relative to $S'$ of type $\mathrm{tys}_K$ at the principal level of $N'$, matching at $S'$ for $\sigma^{-1}$, and with the unit matching condition of `hFLu` holding at every $v \notin S'$ which is unramified in $L$, one has
--   $$\int_{\Phi_L} \int_{\Omega_L} \xi_L(z) \Big( \sum_{\delta \in \mathcal{D}} \varphi\big(x^{-1} \cdot \delta \cdot {}^{\sigma^{-1}}(z x)\big) \Big)\, d\nu_{Z,L}\, d\mu_L \; = \; c \sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \int_{\Phi_K} \int_{\Omega_K} \xi_K(z)\big( \mathrm{K}^{\mathrm{cent}}_f(x, zx) + \mathrm{K}^{\mathrm{ell}}_f(x, zx) \big)\, d\nu_{Z,K}\, d\mu_K,$$
--   where $\delta$ is embedded by `globalPoints`, $z$ acts through the central scalar, ${}^{\sigma^{-1}}(\cdot)$ is the action `sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ.symm`, the inner sum is a finite-support sum over the set $\mathcal{D}$ of those $\delta \in GL_2(L)$ for which there is $\gamma \in GL_2(K)$ lying in the elliptic cell (characteristic polynomial without root in $K$) or in the central cell (scalar matrix) with `normClassMap hgen` of the $\sigma^{-1}$-conjugacy class of $\delta$ equal to the conjugacy class of $\gamma$, and where $\mathrm{K}^{\mathrm{cent}}_f(x,y) = \sum_{\gamma \text{ central}} f(x^{-1}\gamma y)$ and $\mathrm{K}^{\mathrm{ell}}_f(x,y) = \sum_{\gamma \text{ elliptic}} f(x^{-1}\gamma y)$ are the central and elliptic parts of the adelic kernel, the measures $\mu_L$, $\mu_K$ being the adelic Haar measures on $GL_2$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists $c \in \mathbb{C}$ with $c \neq 0$ such that, for every assignment $t$ of a pair of complex numbers $t(w)$ to each prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ subject to the following two conditions, an identity of spectral fibre sums holds.
--
--   The first condition on $t$ excludes Eisenstein data: for every nonzero ideal $M$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ and every pair $\chi_1, \chi_2$ of characters of the ideles of $L$ which are continuous and trivial on the principal ideles, there exists a prime $w \notin S_L$ with $t(w) \neq \big(a_w, b_w\big)$, where $a_w$ and $b_w$ are the values at $w$ of the Eisenstein eigensystem [`LanglandsTunnell.Converse.eisensteinTableOf L M hM χ₁ χ₂`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ConverseData.html#L132), namely $a_w = \chi_1(\varpi_w) + \chi_2(\varpi_w)$ and $b_w = \chi_1(\varpi_w)\chi_2(\varpi_w)$ evaluated on the uniformiser idele at $w$. The second condition is constancy along fibres: $t(w) = t(w')$ whenever $w, w' \notin S_L$ lie over the same prime of $K$.
--
--   The asserted identity is
--   $$\sum_{\Psi}{}' \; \mathrm{twistedCutTrace}\,(\Psi) \; = \; c \sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \; \sum_{\pi}{}' \; \mathrm{cutTrace}\,(\pi),$$
--   in which both inner sums are unconditional sums (`tsum`) over subtypes. On the left, $\Psi$ runs over those Hecke eigensystems for $L$ with complex coefficients which belong to `cuspClasses L` for the production pins `productionPinsOf L ΦL (fun M => levelOne (𝓞 L) L M ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L) (heckeGen (𝓞 L) L) (adelicBox L)`, the character $\xi_L$, the level $N$ and the set $S_L$ — that is, $\Psi$ has level exactly $N$, has $\Psi.a\,w = \Psi.b\,w = 0$ for all $w \in S_L$, and has nonzero isotypic cuspidal span — and which moreover satisfy $(\Psi.a\,w, \Psi.b\,w) = t(w)$ for every $w \notin S_L$; the summand is `twistedCutTrace K L D σ` of these pins, $\xi_L$, $N$, $S_L$, $\Psi$, $\mathrm{tys}_L$, $\varphi$, namely the trace of the $\sigma$-twisted convolution operator attached to $D$ and $\varphi$ on the intersection of the isotypic cuspidal submodule of $\Psi$ with the archimedean cut submodule of $\mathrm{tys}_L$, taken to be $0$ unless that operator preserves the submodule. Note that the twisted trace is formed with $\sigma$, whereas the matching hypotheses are formulated for $\sigma^{-1}$.
--
--   On the right, for each $\xi_K \in \Xi$ the variable $\pi$ runs over those Hecke eigensystems for $K$ which belong to `cuspClasses K` for the production pins `productionPinsOf K (⋃ x ∈ TK, (· * x) '' centreCutSiegelSet K cK uK d₁K d₂K) (fun M => principalLevel (𝓞 K) K M ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K) (heckeGen (𝓞 K) K) (adelicBox K)`, the character $\xi_K$, the level $N'$ and the set $S_K$ — level exactly $N'$, vanishing $a$ and $b$ on $S_K$, nonzero isotypic cuspidal span — and which satisfy $\big((\mathrm{formalBaseChange}\,K\,L\,\pi).a\,w, (\mathrm{formalBaseChange}\,K\,L\,\pi).b\,w\big) = t(w)$ for every prime $w \notin S_L$ of $L$, where the formal base change has level $\top$, $a$-value at $w$ equal to `satakePow` of the inertia degree of $w$ over the prime below applied to the pair $(\pi.a, \pi.b)$ at that prime, and $b$-value the corresponding power of $\pi.b$; the summand is `cutTrace K` of these pins, $\xi_K$, $N'$, $S_K$, $\pi$, $\mathrm{tys}_K$, $f$, the trace of the convolution operator by $f$ on the intersection of the isotypic cuspidal submodule of $\pi$ with the archimedean cut submodule of $\mathrm{tys}_K$, taken to be $0$ unless that operator preserves the submodule. In particular the constant $c$ is independent of $t$.
--
--   This is the passage from the geometric to the spectral side in the comparison of the $\sigma$-twisted trace formula for $GL_2$ over $L$ with the trace formula over $K$, for a Galois extension $L/K$ of prime degree: an identity of central-plus-elliptic geometric terms is converted into an identity between the twisted cut trace summed over cuspidal Hecke eigensystems of $L$ with prescribed non-Eisenstein Satake data $t$ outside $S_L$ and the corresponding sums of cut traces over eigensystems of $K$ whose formal base change realises $t$, the characters of $K$ being those restricting to $\xi_L$ along the idelic norm. It feeds the base-change comparison used in the Langlands–Tunnell input, and is cited by [`AutomorphicForm.fibreSum_twistedCutTrace_eq_const_mul_fibreSum_cutTrace_of_areMatchingAt_symm_of_prime`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.fibreSum_twistedCutTrace_eq_const_mul_fibreSum_cutTrace_of_areMatchingAt_symm_of_prime).
